---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import AiLandingHero from '../../components/AiLandingHero.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { describeServiceHref } from '../../data/contact';

const context = 'AI-assisted service design';
---

<Base
  title="AI-assisted public service design | Registry Stack"
  description="Use research and service requirements to design a government service. Try a prototype with staff and applicants. Your delivery team receives a clear brief."
  ogImagePath="/og-ai.png"
  ogImageAlt="Registry Stack: Design, adapt and access public services with AI."
>
  <SiteHeader current="ai-service-design" />
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <AiLandingHero
      eyebrow="AI-assisted service design"
      heading="Design a service that people can test before it is built."
      lead="AI helps turn your research and service requirements into a brief. Applicants and staff test a prototype before you decide what to build."
      context={context}
      exampleHref="#worked-example"
      exampleLabel="See the school enrolment example"
      exampleNote="Fictional example: a delivery partner’s draft enrolment brief identifies an age check and a rule that the education authority must confirm."
      note="We offer this as a scoped engagement, mainly through our partners."
    >
      <p class="ai-example-label">Example: brief prepared by your delivery partner</p>
      <p class="ai-example-title">School enrolment</p>
      <dl class="ai-example-rows">
        <div><dt>Form item 1</dt><dd>The parent supplies the child’s date of birth.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Proposed change</dt><dd>Ask the civil register if the child meets the age rule.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Decision for the education authority</dt><dd>Which cut-off date applies to this school year?</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </AiLandingHero>

    <section class="section section-muted" id="worked-example" aria-labelledby="example-title">
      <div class="section-inner approach-split">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">School enrolment example</p>
          <h2 id="example-title">See how to help a parent apply for school.</h2>
          <p>A parent brings a form to the school office. The officer enters the child’s date of birth and confirms it with the parent.</p>
          <p>The team tries a prototype that asks an approved civil register for an age check. If the source cannot answer, the screen prompts the officer to review the document with the parent.</p>
          <p>The education authority confirms the age rule. The civil-registration authority decides whether it can offer the check. It also decides what information it can return.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="editorial-callout">
          <h3>Three situations to test</h3>
          <ol class="approach-steps">
            <li><strong>The child qualifies for the local school</strong><span>The service confirms the school assignment. It gives the parent a reference.</span></li>
            <li><strong>The source cannot confirm the child’s age</strong><span>The screen guides the officer through the manual check that your institution has agreed.</span></li>
            <li><strong>The parent requests another school</strong><span>The district officer’s decision is recorded. An authorised person or service applies it to the register. The prototype does not write to the register.</span></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="outputs-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="outputs-title">Your delivery team gets a brief it can build from.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="value-grid">
          <article>
            <h3>See where people need help</h3>
            <p>You work through the planned service with staff and applicants. The brief keeps source references. When you adapt an existing form, it also keeps the form’s item numbers. This lets everyone check each proposed change.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Resolve the questions that affect the build</h3>
            <p>AI helps organise the evidence and flags gaps. The responsible teams confirm which rules apply and which sources can be used. They also confirm who can decide an exception.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Find problems in a prototype</h3>
            <p>Applicants and staff try common and difficult cases. You use what you learn to revise the brief. You also use it to agree what to test in the working service.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="section-note">We offer this design method as a scoped engagement, delivered mainly through our partners. The brief guides <a href="/customization/">how we use AI in implementation</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="next-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2 id="next-title">Discuss the service you need to design.</h2>
        <p>Bring the requirements for a new service, or a form and process you want to adapt. We run service design with our partners. The brief guides a scoped implementation.</p>
        <div class="section-links">
          <a class="button button-primary" href={describeServiceHref(context)} data-journey="service-inquiry">Discuss your service</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/pricing/#process">See how implementation works</a>
        </div>
        <p class="final-cta-note"><a href="/pricing/">See implementation and support options</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Base>
